321: \todo{Remarks cut from Section~II-B; keep here or drop?}
322: \begin{itemize}
323: \item $Y^2$ is realised by repeating $Y$, not as a second scheduling variable $p_2=Y^2$, which would admit pairs with $p_2\neq Y^2$; extra scheduling variables cause overbounding in controller synthesis \cite{drenth2026lpvlfr}
324: \item The scheduling map is a known selection of the state ($Y=q_3$), not a learned map as in the self-scheduled models of \cite{drenth2026lpvlfr}
325: \item The exact condition $\det M(Y)\neq0$ replaces the sufficient condition of \cite[Thm.~6]{drenth2026lpvlfr}, which needs a scheduling set in the unit ball and $\rho(D_{zw})<1$
326: \item Drenth's Def.~1 is stated in discrete time but constrains only the algebraic loop equation, so it applies unchanged in continuous time

